# The last people, from a normal start. Seed 1 wakes beside Oyster Row: walk
# up toward the square with the real keys, wait to see a villager dressed for
# the coast and their trade, walk up beside one on the camera's side, and to the
# village dog. Walk out to the refuse the island dumps and watch its gulls work
# it. Oyster Row busy in the afternoon; the village into the evening (warm by
# its fires, the lantern lit with its key and the slate marking the player),
# everyone indoors at night and out at dawn. Then the villages of the other
# lands, each dressed for its own weather. Last, what a crowd costs on screen.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/characters.tour --seed=1
coast calm
wait 1.0
shot 01-wake
walk 1,-1 0.9
await folk 6
wait 0.4
shot 02-oyster-row with folk
walkto folk 12
zoom 5
wait 0.4
shot 03-a-villager-close with folk
zoom 9
walkto dog 20
zoom 8
await dog 10
wait 0.8
shot 04-the-village-dog with dog
# Gulls over the refuse: the nearest tip or wreck, whatever village is near.
zoom 15
walkto refuse 60
zoom 9
await gulls 40
wait 0.5
shot 05-gulls-on-the-refuse with gulls
# Oyster Row in the afternoon, several out at once.
village 0
hour 15.5
zoom 15
await crowd 20
wait 0.5
shot 06-oyster-row-afternoon with crowd
hour 19.6
wait 2.5
shot 07-dusk
hour 20.7
wait 2.0
tap lamp
wait 1.0
zoom 5
shot 08-lantern-slate-and-rims with lamp
zoom 9
hour 21.02
wait 12
shot 09-indoors
hour 5.6
wait 3
shot 10-dawn
# The other lands: teleports, then the same wait and walk to someone.
hour 11
zoom 12
# Villages are numbered by worldgen and the numbers move: 10 is Pennock on the
# coast now, and this frame has been a picture of green grass and a sandy shore
# called "snowfield" ever since. The `land:` claim is what keeps it honest.
village 12
await folk 8
walkto folk 12
zoom 7
wait 0.5
shot 11-snowfield-hush-fold with folk,land:snowfield
zoom 12
village 8
await folk 8
walkto folk 12
zoom 7
wait 0.5
shot 12-burning-emberlow with folk,land:burning
zoom 12
village 1
await folk 8
walkto folk 12
zoom 7
wait 0.5
shot 13-moss-fennick with folk,land:moss
# What 24 villagers cost drawn on screen, against the same frames without them:
# a budget of 7 draw calls and 1 ms of frame a person.
zoom 15
perf folk 24 3 7 1.0
shot 14-crowd-of-24 with crowd
